From d94b3f7e852ea68c5766e26d88f67f3ab343a012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:47:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tools): a single-form thread mill without a pitch range,
 and the dovetail neck tolerance

A single-form thread mill whose definition has no `pitch_min` key (a
converter that read only the tooth) reads as a range of its one stated
pitch, in the project file, the .camtools reader and the shipped catalog
reader. The thread operation cuts that pitch and refuses every other
pitch by name. A stated 0 and an in-memory record without a range stay
refused. The writer is unchanged, so no version step.

The dovetail neck check takes a 1e-9 mm float-dust slack: an inch
dovetail whose flank meets its neck exactly is no longer refused.

Pins the #3662 synthetic form mill (a necked single-form thread mill
with its drawn cutter) and tapered mills (flat and ball tip) in
.camtools.

Fixes #3662

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
